  "nl_text": "The database schema named \"schemabench_0101\" consists of four tables. The main table is named \"Data\", which contains various data related to countries and indicators. This table has 44 columns, including CountryName, CountryCode, IndicatorName, IndicatorCode, and 38 years worth of data (from 1960 to 2012). The table is structured with CountryCode and IndicatorCode as the primary key, ensuring entity integrity. The Data table has two foreign keys, IndicatorCode and CountryCode, which reference the INDICATOR_CODE and CountryCode from the Metadata-Indicators and Metadata-Countries tables respectively. The DELETE and UPDATE rules are set to CASCADE, which means if a record in the Metadata-Indicators or Metadata-Countries table is deleted or updated, the corresponding records in the Data table will also be deleted or updated.\nThe Metadata-Countries table contains information about countries, including CountryCode, CountryName, Region, IncomeGroup, and SpecialNotes. This table has CountryCode as the primary key.\nThe Metadata-Indicators table contains information about indicators, including INDICATOR_CODE, INDICATOR_NAME, SOURCE_NOTE, and SOURCE_ORGANIZATION. This table has INDICATOR_CODE as the primary key.\nThe target table, which is also related to countries, contains information about the target values for each country in the future. This table has CountryCode as the primary key and a foreign key referencing CountryCode in the Metadata-Countries table. The DELETE and UPDATE rules are set to CASCADE, similar to the Data table.\nIn summary, this schema is designed to manage and analyze data related to countries and indicators, with the aim of predicting future target values.",
  "gold_question": "1) Background / Context\n\nThe project involves developing a predictive analytics system to estimate \"Forest area (% of land area)\" for 247 countries in 2012. The estimation is based on historical data ranging from 1960 to 2011. The data is stored in a structured database format.\n\n2) Objectives\n\n- Accurately predict the percentage of forest area for each specified country in 2012.\n- Utilize historical data from 1960 to 2011 for prediction.\n\n3) Stakeholders & Users\n\n- Environmental analysts who will use the predictions for research and policy-making.\n- Data scientists responsible for developing and refining the prediction model.\n- Government agencies interested in monitoring and managing forest resources.\n\n4) Functional Descriptions\n\n- Extract and preprocess historical data from the database.\n- Develop a predictive model using machine learning techniques to estimate 2012 forest area percentages based on past data.\n- Validate and evaluate the model's accuracy with appropriate metrics.\n- Provide a user interface for analysts to access predictions and assess data.\n\n5) Non-Functional Descriptions\n\n- Ensure data security and integrity throughout the data processing pipeline.\n- Design the system to handle up to 500 concurrent users querying the predictions.\n- Deliver predictions with a latency of no more than 2 seconds per request.",
  "input_json": "/data/SchemaBench/Experiment/schema2text_deepseek/0101.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0101\nCREATE TABLE `data` (\n  `country_code` char(3) NOT NULL,\n  `indicator_code` char(10) NOT NULL,\n  `country_name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `indicator_name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `year_1960` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `year_1961` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `year_1962` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `year_1963` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `year_1964` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `year_1965` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `year_1966` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `year_1967` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `year_1968` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `year_1969` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `year_1970` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `year_1971` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `year_1972` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `year_1973` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `year_1974` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `year_1975` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `year_1976` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `year_1977` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `year_1978` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `year_1979` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `year_1980` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `year_1981` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `year_1982` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `year_1983` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `year_1984` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `year_1985` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `year_1986` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `year_1987` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `year_1988` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `year_1989` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `year_1990` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `year_1991` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `year_1992` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `year_1993` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `year_1994` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `year_1995` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `year_1996` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `year_1997` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `year_1998` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `year_1999` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `year_2000` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `year_2001` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `year_2002` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `year_2003` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `year_2004` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `year_2005` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `year_2006` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `year_2007` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `year_2008` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `year_2009` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `year_2010` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `year_2011` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `year_2012` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`country_code`, `indicator_code`),\n  CONSTRAINT `data_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`indicator_code`) REFERENCES `metadata_indicators` (`indicator_code`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `data_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`country_code`) REFERENCES `metadata_countries` (`country_code`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\nCREATE TABLE `metadata_countries` (\n  `country_code` char(3) NOT NULL,\n  `country_name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `region` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `income_group` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `special_notes` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`country_code`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\nCREATE TABLE `metadata_indicators` (\n  `indicator_code` char(10) NOT NULL,\n  `indicator_name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `source_note` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `source_organization` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`indicator_code`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\nCREATE TABLE `targets` (\n  `country_code` char(3) NOT NULL,\n  `target_value` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`country_code`),\n  CONSTRAINT `targets_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`country_code`) REFERENCES `metadata_countries` (`country_code`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
